WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.848
The Priority Action Approach organizes attention. Start with safety, identify the problem that could harm the patient first, act on it, and then continue gathering information. Saying an acronym without examining or intervening does not complete an assessment.
优先行动法组织的是注意力：先保证安全，识别最先会伤害患者的问题，处理后继续收集信息。只背缩写、没有真正检查或干预，不算完成评估。

00:00:16.848 --> 00:00:31.824
For an apparently well person, conversation and rapport can precede detailed examination. An unwell person needs a rapid formal survey. Either way, your first impression is provisional and must be tested.
对于表面状况良好的人，可以先交流、建立关系，再详细检查。病情不佳者需要快速正式初评。无论哪种情况，第一印象都是待验证判断。

00:00:31.824 --> 00:00:42.648
A partner may obtain measurements while you assess another priority. Name the task and confirm its result; parallel work is not the same as leaving a step to chance.
同伴可以在你评估另一优先问题时测量生命体征。应明确分派并确认结果；并行工作不等于把某一步交给运气。

00:00:42.648 --> 00:00:54.864
This lesson follows the seven sections of school 7A. The laboratory timing targets are practice expectations; current service guidance and the patient determine clinical actions.
本课覆盖学校 7A 的七个部分。实验室计时目标属于练习要求；临床行动仍由现行机构指导及患者实际情况决定。

00:00:54.864 --> 00:01:09.096
Before approaching, scan the area and your route back to the ambulance. Ask what could change once you are committed beside the patient: a closing door, an aggressive bystander, traffic or an unstable surface.
接近前观察现场及返回救护车的路线。考虑到达患者身旁后什么可能变化：关上的门、激动旁观者、交通或不稳地面。

00:01:09.096 --> 00:01:21.072
Count patients rather than accepting the dispatch count as final. Identify whether fire, police, rescue or an additional clinical crew is needed, and request them early.
不要把调度报告人数当作最终人数，应自己清点。判断是否需要消防、警察、救援或额外医护团队，并尽早请求。

00:01:21.072 --> 00:01:36.024
Choose precautions from the actual exposure risk before contact. Gloves do not protect against every hazard and do not replace hand hygiene. An uncontrolled hazard is a reason to remain at a safe distance, not to hurry through it.
接触前依据实际暴露风险选择防护。手套不能防所有危险，也不能代替手卫生。危险无法控制时，应保持安全距离，而不是赶快冲进去。

00:01:36.024 --> 00:01:45.840
Recheck scene safety during treatment and departure. A safe arrival does not guarantee a safe move down the stairs or a safe return through the same doorway.
处理和离场时继续评估安全。到达时安全，不代表下楼搬运或从原门返回时仍安全。

00:01:45.840 --> 00:02:00.432
Mechanism of injury describes the forces or event associated with trauma. Nature of illness describes the medical problem being investigated. The two can coexist: a medical collapse can cause a traumatic fall.
受伤机制描述创伤相关的力量或事件；疾病性质描述正在调查的内科问题。两者可能并存，例如疾病导致晕倒，再造成跌伤。

00:02:00.432 --> 00:02:12.336
Medication packaging suggests questions, not proof that a drug was taken today. A walker suggests asking about baseline mobility, not assuming that current weakness is usual.
药物包装提示需要询问，但不能证明今天服药了。助行器提示应询问平日活动能力，不能据此认定今天虚弱也是常态。

00:02:12.336 --> 00:02:23.856
Ask a witness what they saw, when the patient was last functioning normally and what changed. Attribute the account to that witness and retain uncertainty about unobserved events.
询问目击者实际看见什么、患者最后正常活动时间以及出现了什么变化。记录信息来源，对无人目睹的事情保留不确定性。

00:02:23.856 --> 00:02:34.272
Several occupants with headache and nausea should redirect attention to a shared environmental exposure. Do not enter an unsafe building to obtain a better history.
多人同时头痛、恶心，应把注意力转向共同环境暴露。不能为获得更完整病史而进入不安全建筑。

00:02:34.272 --> 00:02:44.568
Look before touching. A person unable to finish a sentence, slumping with poor tone or becoming confused is not made safe by a reassuring dispatch label.
接触前先观察。无法说完整句子、瘫软坐倒或开始意识混乱者，不会因为调度标签听起来不严重就变得安全。

00:02:44.568 --> 00:02:56.808
If there is life-threatening external hemorrhage, arrange immediate control before the formal survey continues. Do not wait until the letter C simply because a memorized sequence places it later.
发现致命外出血，应立即安排控制，再继续正式初评。不能因为背诵顺序把 C 放在后面，就等到那时才处理。

00:02:56.808 --> 00:03:10.968
An unconscious patient requires breathing and circulation to be assessed together, with the arrest pathway activated when indicated. A slow, rigid airway-first recital must not delay chest compressions.
无意识患者需要同时评估呼吸与循环，符合条件立即进入骤停流程。缓慢、机械地先背完气道步骤，不能延误胸外按压。

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:24.264
State your concern aloud and delegate. For example: this patient looks critically unwell; bring the resuscitation equipment and prepare for urgent movement while we assess immediate threats.
把担忧说出来并分工。例如：“患者看起来非常危重；带来复苏设备，在我们评估即时威胁时准备紧急搬运。”

00:03:24.264 --> 00:03:39.240
Introduce yourself if the person can engage, and assess spontaneous alertness and response to voice. AVPU is a rapid coarse description: alert, voice, pressure or pain response, and unresponsive.
患者可以交流时先介绍自己，评估自发清醒及对声音反应。AVPU 是快速粗略描述：清醒、声音反应、压力或疼痛反应、无反应。

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:50.952
A detailed Glasgow Coma Scale assessment comes next when appropriate. Report its components rather than guessing a total from a greeting or labelling every confused person intoxicated.
适当时进一步做详细 GCS 评估。应报告各分项，不能从一句问候猜出总分，也不能把每位意识混乱者都归为醉酒。

00:03:50.952 --> 00:04:06.264
When trauma or the mechanism raises spinal concern, delegate suitable movement control. Opening an obstructed airway and effective resuscitation remain priorities; do not maintain a dangerous position just to avoid all movement.
创伤或机制提示脊柱风险时，分派适当动作控制。解除气道梗阻和有效复苏仍优先；不能为绝对不动而维持危险体位。

00:04:06.264 --> 00:04:18.960
Do not practise painful stimuli on classmates. In simulation, verbalize the assessment and use the instructor-approved response cue; practical technique requires direct supervision.
不要在同学身上练习疼痛刺激。模拟时口述评估并使用教师批准的反应提示；具体技术需要现场督导。

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:33.504
A speaking patient demonstrates airflow at that moment, but this does not guarantee continuing patency. Listen for changing voice, gurgling, snoring or stridor, and look for blood, vomit or swelling.
能够说话表示此刻有气流，但不能保证气道持续通畅。注意声音改变、咕噜声、鼾声或喉鸣，并观察血液、呕吐物或肿胀。

00:04:33.504 --> 00:04:45.816
Use the airway-opening approach appropriate to the clinical situation and your training. Clear obstructing material with approved methods and suction when indicated; do not perform blind finger sweeps.
按临床情况及受训内容选择开放气道方式。用获准方法清除阻塞物，需要时吸引；不要盲目手指探扫。

00:04:45.816 --> 00:04:59.304
An OPA or NPA is considered according to responsiveness, protective reflexes, anatomy and contraindications. Reduced consciousness alone does not authorize either device without assessment.
选择 OPA 或 NPA 时，应考虑反应程度、保护反射、解剖和禁忌。单凭意识下降，不能不评估就放入任一器械。

00:04:59.304 --> 00:05:09.960
Immediately reassess whether air moves. Preparing a device, inserting it or announcing airway clear is not equivalent to demonstrating a functioning airway.
立即再评估是否有气流。准备器械、放入器械或口述“气道通畅”，都不等于证明气道确实有效。

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:21.552
Observe actual chest rise and respiratory effort. Six shallow breaths per minute in an unresponsive adult is a ventilation problem even before a monitor produces a number.
观察真实胸廓起伏及呼吸用力。无反应成人每分钟六次浅呼吸，即使监护仪尚未显示数值，也已经是通气问题。

00:05:21.552 --> 00:05:35.496
Supplemental oxygen can improve saturation without correcting carbon dioxide retention. If ventilation is inadequate, support it with the trained bag-mask technique and reassess chest rise and air movement.
补氧可能改善血氧饱和度，却不纠正二氧化碳潴留。通气不足时，应按受训球囊面罩技术辅助通气，再评估胸廓起伏和气流。

00:05:35.496 --> 00:05:48.336
The school uses respiratory-rate extremes as red flags. An apparently ordinary rate with tiny tidal volumes, exhaustion or irregular pauses can still represent respiratory failure.
学校把呼吸频率极端值作为警示。频率看似平常，但潮气量极小、疲竭或不规则暂停，仍可能是呼吸衰竭。

00:05:48.336 --> 00:06:01.728
Give indicated oxygen without delaying care to obtain a room-air reading. Device choice and oxygen targets must follow the relevant current clinical guidance, not an automatic maximum for every patient.
需要给氧时，不要为获得室内空气读数而延误照护。装置及目标应依据相应现行临床指导，而不是人人自动使用最大氧量。

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:12.744
Palpate an appropriate pulse and correlate it with the patient, not only the displayed heart rate. Electrical activity on a monitor does not prove mechanical circulation.
在适当部位触诊脉搏，并结合患者状态，而不是只看显示心率。监护仪有电活动，不证明存在机械循环。

00:06:12.744 --> 00:06:23.280
Major visible hemorrhage should already be controlled. Recheck the effectiveness of pressure, packing or a tourniquet as appropriate to training, especially after movement.
明显大出血此时应已得到处理。按受训内容复查直接加压、填塞或止血带效果，特别是在搬动后。

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:35.112
A palpable radial pulse cannot be converted into a reliable systolic pressure. Nor does it prove adequate brain perfusion; compare alertness, skin and serial measurements.
可触及桡动脉不能换算成可靠的收缩压，也不能证明脑灌注足够；应结合清醒程度、皮肤及连续测量。

00:06:35.112 --> 00:06:48.288
Shock means inadequate tissue perfusion, not simply low blood pressure. Compensatory vasoconstriction and tachycardia can preserve the pressure while the patient is becoming more unwell.
休克是组织灌注不足，不只是低血压。代偿性血管收缩和心率加快，可以在患者逐渐恶化时暂时维持血压。

00:06:48.288 --> 00:06:58.368
The rapid body survey is a brief search for important hidden injury, tailored to the presentation. It is not the detailed secondary head-to-toe examination.
快速全身检查是针对患者表现，简短寻找重要隐藏损伤，不是详细的次级头到脚检查。

00:06:58.368 --> 00:07:24.144
Inspect and gently assess systematically, including blood on your gloves and concealed surfaces when safe access is possible. The school also names subcutaneous emphysema: air in tissue under the skin, potentially felt as crackling around the chest or neck. Report the finding and assess related breathing or injury concerns; a rapid sweep does not exclude internal injury.
系统观察和轻柔检查，注意手套血迹，并在安全可及情况下检查遮蔽部位。学校还点名皮下气肿，即皮下组织内有空气，胸颈部可能触及捻发感。应报告发现并评估相关呼吸或损伤担忧；快速扫查不能排除内伤。

00:07:24.144 --> 00:07:38.184
Do not repeatedly spring or rock a suspected injured pelvis to prove instability. Avoid unnecessary manipulation of fractures; arrange appropriate stabilization and movement with trained supervision.
怀疑骨盆损伤时，不要反复弹压或摇动来证明不稳定。避免不必要地操弄骨折；在受训督导下安排适当固定和搬运。

00:07:38.184 --> 00:07:52.344
The school describes an approximately thirty-second rapid survey and a primary survey within two minutes when no intervention is needed. These are fluency targets, not reasons to omit a threat or delay necessary care.
学校描述快速全身检查约三十秒，无需干预时初评两分钟内完成。这是熟练度目标，不是遗漏威胁或延误必要照护的理由。

00:07:52.344 --> 00:08:08.352
In school 7A, SOAPPP means skin, oxygen, airway adjunct, pupils, pressure or bleeding, and position or packaging. Use it as a final omission check, not a second primary survey performed from the beginning.
学校 7A 中 SOAPPP 指皮肤、氧气、气道辅助器械、瞳孔、加压或出血、体位或包装。它是最后查漏，不是从头再做一遍初评。

00:08:08.352 --> 00:08:22.032
Ask whether each intervention is needed and effective now. Oxygen may need titration; an adjunct may become inappropriate if protective reflexes return; bleeding can recur after movement.
逐项问现在是否仍需要、是否有效。氧气可能需要滴定；保护反射恢复后辅助器械可能不再合适；搬动后可能再次出血。

00:08:22.032 --> 00:08:34.920
Packaging includes warmth, secure equipment, suitable positioning and a movement plan. The priority is safe, effective departure rather than making every strap and monitor lead look perfect first.
包装包括保暖、设备固定、适当体位及搬运计划。重点是安全有效地离场，而不是先让每条束带和导线都看起来完美。

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:47.880
The current saved provincial exam list also names bandaging, pelvic binding and blankets. Learn both source-specific lists instead of assuming the school acronym reproduces every licensing item.
现存省考试指南列表还明确列出包扎、骨盆固定及保温毯。应分别学习两个来源的清单，不能认为学校缩写已经复现所有执照考试项目。

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:59.952
After initial life threats are addressed, state whether this is a rapid-transport-category patient in the school framework. The decision is based on the whole presentation and can change.
处理初始生命威胁后，应按学校框架明确是否属于快速转运类别。决定依据整体表现，而且可以变化。

00:08:59.952 --> 00:09:11.328
A major injury can need urgent definitive care despite a normal initial pressure. Conversely, a medical emergency can be unstable without a traumatic mechanism.
重大损伤即使初始血压正常，也可能需要紧急确定性治疗。反过来，内科急症即使没有创伤机制，也可能不稳定。

00:09:11.328 --> 00:09:22.800
Give the reason and the operational consequence: urgent transport because of poor perfusion; essential hemorrhage and airway work now; remaining history during safe conveyance.
说明理由及行动后果：“因灌注不良需要紧急转运；现在完成必要止血和气道处理，其余病史在安全转运中采集。”

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:32.040
The destination follows the relevant regional clinical pathway and resources, not simply the nearest building or the existence of a particular acronym.
目的地应依据相应地区临床路径及资源，而不是只选最近建筑，或只依据某个缩写。

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:45.768
School 7A highlights penetrating injuries to the head, neck, torso or limbs proximal to the elbow or knee. The concern is damage to major structures and bleeding not visible from the wound size.
学校 7A 强调头、颈、躯干及肘膝近端的穿透伤。担忧的是重要结构损伤和隐藏出血，伤口大小不能反映全部风险。

00:09:45.768 --> 00:09:59.040
Chest-wall instability, pelvic injury and two or more proximal long-bone fractures can represent serious injury and concealed blood loss. Normal initial measurements do not cancel those risks.
胸壁不稳定、骨盆损伤和两处或以上近端长骨骨折，可能代表严重损伤及隐匿失血。初始测量正常不能取消这些风险。

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:10.248
A crushed, degloved, mangled or pulseless limb and an amputation proximal to the wrist or ankle require urgent attention to limb and systemic threats.
挤压、脱套、严重毁损、无脉肢体，以及腕踝近端截肢，都需要紧急关注肢体及全身威胁。

00:10:10.248 --> 00:10:24.312
The provincial examination document adds other unstable findings, including new neurological deficits and major burns. A source list is not a reason to ignore an equally serious finding absent from a school slide.
省考试文件还列出新发神经缺损和重大烧伤等不稳定表现。不能因为某严重发现未出现在学校某页，就不予重视。

00:10:24.312 --> 00:10:39.648
The school gives GCS below fourteen and systolic pressure below ninety as numeric RTC cues. Its respiratory examples include fewer than ten or more than thirty breaths per minute, with inconsistent wording about accompanying shock.
学校给出 GCS 小于十四、收缩压小于九十等数字性 RTC 提示。呼吸示例包括每分钟少于十次或多于三十次，但是否要求伴休克的文字并不一致。

00:10:39.648 --> 00:10:51.672
Do not interpret that ambiguity as permission to wait for shock before treating severe respiratory distress. Assess adequacy, effort, mentation and the patient's trajectory.
不能把这种歧义理解成必须等出现休克才处理严重呼吸窘迫。应评估呼吸是否足够、用力、意识及变化方向。

00:10:51.672 --> 00:11:05.472
The licensing document treats altered consciousness, airway difficulty, respiratory distress and several time-critical medical syndromes as unstable findings without requiring those exact school thresholds.
执照考试文件把意识改变、气道维持困难、呼吸窘迫及多种时间紧迫内科综合征列为不稳定表现，并不要求先达到学校这些精确阈值。

00:11:05.472 --> 00:11:16.464
A change from a personal baseline matters. New confusion with a pressure of one hundred and twenty is still concerning, and shock can be present before a pressure falls below ninety.
偏离个人基线也很重要。血压一百二十但新发意识混乱，仍值得担忧；休克可以在收缩压跌破九十前出现。

00:11:16.464 --> 00:11:31.296
Learn the school mechanism examples as assigned: an adult fall above twenty feet, and a child fall above ten feet or roughly two to three body heights. These are school triage cues, not a guarantee of safety below them.
按要求学习学校机制示例：成人超过二十英尺跌落，儿童超过十英尺或约身高两到三倍。这些是学校分流提示，低于它们并不保证安全。

00:11:31.296 --> 00:11:58.704
Vehicle ejection, a death in the same compartment and major intrusion indicate substantial energy. School 7A names more than twelve inches of intrusion at the occupant site and a motorcycle crash above thirty kilometres per hour. Preserve those school examples alongside the provincial values on the next segment. Ask where the patient sat and how the body moved; a photograph alone does not establish the injury.
车辆抛出、同车厢有人死亡及重大侵入变形，提示高能量。学校7A点名乘员位置侵入超过十二英寸，以及超过每小时三十公里的摩托车碰撞。应把这些学校示例与下一段省指南数值分别保留。须询问患者座位及身体如何运动；照片本身不能确立损伤。

00:11:58.704 --> 00:12:13.512
The saved provincial guideline specifies adult free fall above six metres, intrusion above point three metres on the occupant side or point five metres elsewhere, and high-risk road impacts. Keep units attached to the numbers.
现存省指南列出成人超过六米自由坠落、乘员侧侵入超过零点三米或其他部位超过零点五米，以及高危道路撞击。记数字时必须保留单位。

00:12:13.512 --> 00:12:26.136
A low-energy fall in a frail older adult can still cause major injury or follow a serious medical event. Mechanism supplements physiology and examination; it never replaces them.
虚弱老年人的低能量跌倒仍可能造成重大损伤，或由严重疾病引起。机制是生理及检查的补充，不能取代它们。

00:12:26.136 --> 00:12:44.808
School 7A repeatedly uses fifteen minutes as its RTC scene-time benchmark. Do not call it an absolute BC legal rule: current BCEHS A01 and A02 emphasize meaningful interventions and minimizing scene time, not that universal deadline.
学校 7A 反复把十五分钟作为 RTC 现场时间标准。不能称为绝对的卑诗法律规定：现行 BCEHS A01、A02 强调有意义的干预及缩短现场时间，而非统一绝对时限。

00:12:44.808 --> 00:12:56.424
Fifteen minutes is not permission to remain until the timer expires. If essential support and safe packaging are complete, proceed according to urgency and the transport plan.
十五分钟不是允许一直留到计时结束。必要支持及安全包装已经完成，就应依据紧迫程度及转运计划行动。

00:12:56.424 --> 00:13:08.784
Neither should a deadline cause unsafe extrication or abandonment of essential resuscitation. Communicate barriers, request help and document the actual reason for unavoidable delay.
时限也不能造成不安全脱困，或放弃必要复苏。应沟通障碍、请求协助，并记录无法避免延误的真实原因。

00:13:08.784 --> 00:13:21.384
Do not blindly defer every vital sign. A delegated measurement that immediately changes management may be meaningful now; a long nonessential task should not postpone definitive care.
不要机械地把所有生命体征都推迟。能立即改变处置的分派测量，此刻可能很有意义；冗长且非必要的任务则不应延误确定性治疗。

00:13:21.384 --> 00:13:35.472
Before lifting, decide how the patient can be moved with the least additional risk. Consider consciousness, ventilation, pain, suspected injuries, body size, route restrictions and available personnel.
抬举前，决定怎样以最低额外风险搬运。考虑意识、通气、疼痛、疑似损伤、体型、路线限制和可用人员。

00:13:35.472 --> 00:13:48.624
Assign a movement leader, agree on commands and specify when anyone should stop. Use the approved device within its limits; enthusiasm cannot replace adequate staff or equipment.
指定搬运指挥，约定口令及任何人何时应喊停。使用获准设备并遵守限制；积极性不能替代足够人手和器械。

00:13:48.624 --> 00:14:00.336
Choose a position the patient can tolerate without worsening the clinical threat. A standard diagram does not override vomiting, respiratory distress or the need for resuscitation.
选择患者能够耐受、不会加重临床威胁的体位。标准示意图不能凌驾于呕吐、呼吸窘迫或复苏需要之上。

00:14:00.336 --> 00:14:13.560
Reassess immediately after movement: airway, ventilation, perfusion, symptoms, bleeding control and device function. A previously effective treatment can fail during loading.
搬动后立即复评气道、通气、灌注、症状、止血效果及设备功能。此前有效的处理，可能在装车时失效。

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:25.128
For the school prone-patient exercise, begin with what is actually known: a person is face down and not responding. Do not invent a fall or intoxication as the established cause.
学校俯卧患者练习应从已知事实开始：有人面朝下、无反应。不要凭空把跌倒或醉酒当作已确定原因。

00:14:25.128 --> 00:14:39.336
After safety, rapidly evaluate response and accessible signs of breathing and circulation. Obtain help and arrange a coordinated move when needed to open the airway, assess properly or resuscitate.
安全确认后，快速评估反应及可观察的呼吸循环迹象。需要开放气道、充分检查或复苏时，请求协助并安排协调翻身。

00:14:39.336 --> 00:14:54.096
In the supervised station, identify the leader, protect alignment as practicable, coordinate shoulders, trunk and pelvis, and stop for a problem. Do not independently improvise a one-person roll from this text.
督导站点中，应确定指挥，在可行范围保护身体对线，协调肩、躯干和骨盆，出现问题立即停。不能单凭文字自行发明单人翻身。

00:14:54.096 --> 00:15:06.480
Once positioned, immediately reassess and treat findings. A glucose measurement and neurological examination are important, but neither precedes needed ventilation or CPR.
调整体位后立即复评并处理发现。血糖和神经检查很重要，但不能先于必要通气或心肺复苏。

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:17.160
Start with an open account: what happened today and what is different from usual? Then use SAMPLE to check omissions rather than interrupting the story after every word.
先开放询问：“今天发生了什么？与平常有什么不同？”再用 SAMPLE 查漏，而不是患者每说一句就打断。

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:31.272
For allergies, record the substance and reaction, not only yes or no. For medications, ask about actual use, dose timing, recent changes, nonprescription products and substances relevant to the presentation.
过敏应记录物质及反应，而不只是有或没有。药物应询问实际使用、服药时间、近期改变、非处方产品及与表现有关的其他物质。

00:15:31.272 --> 00:15:43.320
Past history should be pertinent, while last oral intake and events may explain risk or guide later care. Clarify whether the last meal was missed rather than assuming a normal schedule.
既往史应抓相关重点；最后进食及事件经过可能解释风险或指导后续照护。应核实是否漏餐，而不是假定按时吃饭。

00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:53.376
When the patient cannot answer, use a witness or caregiver and label the source. Not known is different from no history, no medication or no allergy.
患者无法回答时，可向目击者或照护者询问，并标明来源。“未知”不同于“没有病史、没有用药或没有过敏”。

00:15:53.376 --> 00:16:03.912
Ask when the symptom began, whether onset was sudden or gradual, and what the patient was doing. Distinguish onset time from the time the ambulance was called.
询问症状开始时间、突然还是逐渐，以及当时在做什么。区分发病时间与呼叫救护车时间。

00:16:03.912 --> 00:16:16.512
Ask what worsens or relieves it, what it feels like, where it is and whether it travels. Avoid suggesting the answer: tell me what it feels like is better than it is just a sharp pain, right?
询问加重或缓解因素、感觉性质、部位及是否放射。避免诱导答案；“请描述什么感觉”优于“就是刺痛，对吧？”

00:16:16.512 --> 00:16:27.576
Use an appropriate severity scale, then ask how the symptom changed over time and what activity it now prevents. A numeric score alone does not describe the clinical problem.
选用适当严重度量表，再询问随时间如何变化，以及现在阻碍什么活动。一个数字不能完整描述临床问题。

00:16:27.576 --> 00:16:41.952
A painless or low-pain presentation does not exclude serious disease. Link symptom characteristics with examination, risk context and associated findings rather than using one reassuring answer to stop.
无痛或轻痛不能排除严重疾病。应把症状特点与检查、风险背景和伴随发现联系起来，而不是得到一个安心答案就停止评估。

00:16:41.952 --> 00:16:51.936
School 7A uses PASTMED for dyspnea. Ask what provoked the problem and whether it is progressing, then ask about chest pain, cough and sputum.
学校 7A 用 PASTMED 询问呼吸困难。先问诱发因素及是否持续加重，再问胸痛、咳嗽及痰。

00:16:51.936 --> 00:17:03.480
Clarify timing and any trauma. Ask which medication was actually used, when it was taken and whether it helped; an inhaler nearby does not establish the response.
明确时间及是否创伤。询问实际用了什么药、何时使用及是否有效；附近有吸入器不能证明用药反应。

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:17.328
Compare current exercise tolerance with the patient's own baseline, including usual oxygen use and prior diagnosis. Ask about fever, allergens, leg symptoms or other relevant associated concerns.
把当前活动耐受与患者个人基线比较，包括平时用氧及既往诊断。按相关性询问发热、过敏原、腿部症状及其他伴随问题。

00:17:17.328 --> 00:17:29.448
Ask short questions if speech is limited, and obtain collateral history while another clinician supports breathing. Finishing the mnemonic is never more important than adequate ventilation.
说话受限时使用简短问题，并在另一临床人员支持呼吸时采集旁证。把缩写问完，永远没有足够通气重要。

00:17:29.448 --> 00:17:40.944
A functional inquiry is a targeted review of related systems, not just asking how well the patient walks. It can reveal an associated symptom the patient did not think to mention.
系统功能询问是针对相关系统的症状回顾，不只是问患者能走多远。它可能发现患者没想到要主动提及的伴随症状。

00:17:40.944 --> 00:17:53.616
With abdominal pain, ask about vomiting or stool blood, urinary symptoms, pregnancy possibility and previous surgery as relevant. Keep questions respectful and privacy appropriate.
腹痛时，按相关性询问呕吐或便血、泌尿症状、怀孕可能及手术史。提问应尊重患者并保护适当隐私。

00:17:53.616 --> 00:18:08.784
With altered consciousness, establish baseline and last-known-well, investigate hypoxia and glucose, and consider trauma, stroke, seizures, infection and toxic exposure. Do not close on one scene clue.
意识改变时，明确基线及最后正常时间，调查低氧和血糖，并考虑创伤、卒中、癫痫、感染和毒物暴露。不要只凭一个现场线索定论。

00:18:08.784 --> 00:18:20.904
A red flag changes urgency; a negative answer changes probability but does not prove absence. Explain which answer would change your next examination or transport decision.
警示征象会改变紧迫程度；否定回答改变可能性，但不证明疾病不存在。应解释哪个答案会改变下一步检查或转运决定。

00:18:20.904 --> 00:18:33.024
A focused examination is not permission to inspect only the painful spot. For an injured wrist after a collapse, the collapse may require a broader assessment than the wrist itself.
重点检查不等于只看疼痛位置。晕倒后手腕受伤者，晕倒原因可能需要比手腕本身更广泛的评估。

00:18:33.024 --> 00:18:46.200
Use a systematic complete examination when major trauma, altered mentation or uncertainty makes hidden findings plausible. Adapt the depth and location of the exam to transport urgency.
重大创伤、意识改变或不确定情况使隐藏异常成为可能时，应系统全面检查。检查深度及地点应适应转运紧迫程度。

00:18:46.200 --> 00:19:00.456
Explain what you need to examine and why, obtain appropriate permission, and limit exposure. Observe, feel and listen as relevant; compare bilateral findings and distal function when injury suggests it.
解释需要检查哪里、为什么，并取得适当同意，限制暴露。按相关性看、触、听，损伤提示需要时比较双侧及远端功能。

00:19:00.456 --> 00:19:09.720
An examination should test a clinical question. State what a finding supports, what it cannot exclude and what you still need to investigate.
检查应检验具体临床问题。应说明某发现支持什么、不能排除什么，以及仍需调查什么。

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:21.768
Repeat the primary priorities, compare the patient with the previous examination and recheck each intervention. Ask what changed, what should have changed and whether anything became worse.
重复主要优先评估，与前次检查比较，并复查每项干预。问：“改变了什么？本来应该改变什么？有没有变得更差？”

00:19:21.768 --> 00:19:44.592
School 7A teaches five-minute unstable and fifteen-minute stable reassessment. Older A01 uses a fifteen-minute minimum, but the new documentation section has selected thirty-minute, fifteen-minute and more frequent categories. The monitoring lesson explains this publication conflict; confirm the applicable service instruction.
学校 7A 教不稳定者五分钟、稳定者十五分钟复评。较旧 A01 使用十五分钟最低要求，但新版记录部分有特定三十分钟、十五分钟及更频繁类别。监测课解释这一出版冲突，实际需确认适用机构要求。

00:19:44.592 --> 00:19:56.472
These intervals are not waiting periods. New confusion, pain, a breathing change, an intervention, movement or an equipment alarm triggers reassessment immediately.
这些间隔不是等待时间。新发混乱、疼痛、呼吸变化、实施干预、搬动或设备警报，都应立即触发复评。

00:19:56.472 --> 00:20:06.408
Record actual values and their times. A line saying stable cannot show a falling pressure, rising respiratory rate or failed response to treatment.
记录实际数值和时间。一句“稳定”无法展示血压下降、呼吸频率上升或治疗无效。

00:20:06.408 --> 00:20:17.424
An initial explanation is useful only while it fits the evidence. Alcohol on the scene does not exclude hypoglycemia, head injury, hypoxia or stroke.
初步解释只有符合证据时才有用。现场有酒精，不能排除低血糖、头部损伤、低氧或卒中。

00:20:17.424 --> 00:20:29.664
Actively seek a finding that could contradict your leading impression. If you believe anxiety explains breathlessness, ask what would suggest a dangerous respiratory or circulatory cause instead.
主动寻找可能反驳主要判断的发现。如果认为焦虑解释了气促，应问什么会提示更危险的呼吸或循环原因。

00:20:29.664 --> 00:20:40.728
Task fixation can look like technical excellence: a perfect splint while perfusion worsens. Periodically ask whether the current task still deserves the team's time.
任务固着可能看起来技术很出色：夹板固定完美，但灌注不断恶化。应定时问当前任务是否仍值得占用团队时间。

00:20:40.728 --> 00:20:51.792
A cognitive pause is brief and targeted. It does not stop needed resuscitation; it prevents an untested assumption from controlling every later decision.
认知暂停应简短、有针对性。它不应停止必要复苏，而是防止未经验证的假设控制所有后续决定。

00:20:51.792 --> 00:21:04.608
This original practice variant mirrors the type of reasoning required in the school older-fall case; it is not a school assessment answer. Ask whether illness caused the fall and what happened afterward.
这个原创变式练习对应学校老年跌倒案例要求的推理类型，不是学校考核答案。应问是否疾病导致跌倒，以及跌倒后发生了什么。

00:21:04.608 --> 00:21:20.592
A caregiver reports new confusion, while the patient reports hip pain. Both accounts matter. Establish baseline, head impact, anticoagulant use, preceding dizziness, infection symptoms and time on the floor.
照护者说新发混乱，患者说髋痛，两种信息都重要。明确基线、头部撞击、抗凝用药、此前头晕、感染症状及倒地时长。

00:21:20.592 --> 00:21:35.832
Check immediate threats, actual vital signs, glucose and relevant neurological and injury findings. Do not force weight bearing to prove a fracture, and do not let a low total NEWS2 cancel a significant red flag.
检查即时威胁、实际生命体征、血糖及相关神经和损伤发现。不要强迫负重来证明骨折，也不能让较低 NEWS2 总分取消重要警示征象。

00:21:35.832 --> 00:21:48.264
State the movement and transport plan, reassess after packaging, and report uncertainty. The receiving clinician needs the new confusion and trajectory, not only the label mechanical fall.
说明搬运和转运计划，包装后复评，并报告不确定性。接收医护人员需要知道新发混乱及变化，而不只是“机械性跌倒”这个标签。

00:21:48.264 --> 00:22:01.056
Record scene context, initial findings and the transport decision with its reason. Add a timed history, examination and measured observations rather than simply marking every system normal.
记录现场背景、初始发现、转运决定及理由。补充有时间的病史、检查和测量，而不是把每个系统直接勾成正常。

00:22:01.056 --> 00:22:15.432
Keep a patient statement distinct from observation: the patient reports dizziness; you observe pallor. A working impression is legitimate when labelled and supported, not presented as an established diagnosis.
区分患者陈述与观察：“患者自诉头晕”；你观察到苍白。初步判断只要明确标注并有依据，可以记录，但不能写成已确诊。

00:22:15.432 --> 00:22:24.384
Pair actions with response and time. Document what could not be obtained and why; never invent a number to make the record complete.
把行动与反应和时间配对。记录无法获得的内容及原因；绝不能为让病历完整而编造数字。

00:22:24.384 --> 00:22:37.056
End with the receiving clinician, time, important unresolved concerns and transfer acceptance. Documentation and ongoing reassessment continue while waiting for formal handover.
结尾应含接收医护人员、时间、重要未解决担忧及交接接收。等待正式交接时，仍需继续记录和再评估。

00:22:37.056 --> 00:22:53.400
NEWS2 structures adult observations using respiratory rate, oxygen saturation, systolic blood pressure, pulse, temperature and consciousness or new confusion. Learn the components and time of each observation, not only the total.
NEWS2 用呼吸频率、血氧饱和度、收缩压、脉搏、体温及意识或新发混乱来结构化成人观察。要掌握各项观察及时间，而不只是总分。

00:22:53.400 --> 00:23:21.384
Record supplemental oxygen status, device and flow. The saved school 7A narrative says one oxygen point, but the Royal College of Physicians NEWS2 chart adds two. Use the correct chart rather than combining the two versions, and ask the instructor to clarify the school discrepancy. Select the saturation scale and treatment target under the applicable clinical guidance; a score does not choose an oxygen target.
应记录是否补氧、装置及流量。保存的学校7A正文把补氧写成一分，但英国皇家内科医师学会NEWS2评分表规定另加两分。应使用正确评分表，不能混合两个版本，并请教师澄清学校差异。血氧量表及治疗目标须按适用临床指导选择；评分不会替你决定氧疗目标。

00:23:21.384 --> 00:23:42.336
NEWS2 is not a pediatric score. School 7A introduces PEWS through behavior, cardiovascular status and respiratory effort. Children need the current age-specific PEWS reference taught in the school pediatric block. Do not apply adult NEWS2 thresholds or assume one age band fits every child.
NEWS2不是儿童评分。学校7A通过行为、心血管状态及呼吸用力三个领域介绍PEWS。儿童应使用学校儿科教学周所教的现行年龄分层PEWS参考。不要套用成人NEWS2阈值，也不要假设一个年龄段适用于所有儿童。

00:23:42.336 --> 00:23:59.064
Use scores to summarize a trend and communicate concern, never to diagnose, rule out deterioration or cancel a red flag. Reassess and escalate a significant change under current service direction even when a total appears reassuring.
评分用于概括趋势和传达担忧，不能用于确诊、排除恶化或取消警示征象。即使总分看似安心，显著变化仍应按现行机构指引复评并升级。

00:23:59.064 --> 00:24:13.224
First complete the clinically necessary assessment and write down what was actually observed or measured, with its time. A score is a way to organize information; calculating one must not delay an immediate response.
先完成临床必要评估，并记录实际观察或测量结果及时间。评分用于组织信息；计算评分不得延误即时处置。

00:24:13.224 --> 00:24:29.352
Choose the tool for the patient group and use its exact approved chart. In this school module, NEWS2 is the adult example and PEWS is the pediatric example. Do not apply adult thresholds to a child or combine different versions into a new chart.
按患者群体选择工具，并使用确切获准的评分表。本校模块中，NEWS2 是成人示例，PEWS 是儿科示例。不得把成人阈值套用到儿童，也不得混合不同版本拼出新表。

00:24:29.352 --> 00:24:47.832
Follow the selected chart’s age band, units, oxygen conditions and parameter definitions. Enter each required observation separately; if something is unavailable or cannot be assessed, report that limitation instead of inventing a value or treating it as normal.
遵循所选评分表的年龄分组、单位、供氧条件及参数定义。逐项输入所需观察；若某项无法取得或评估，应说明局限，不能编造数值或当作正常。

00:24:47.832 --> 00:25:09.216
Read both any single high-risk domain and the aggregate using that same chart’s escalation instructions. Communicate the score with the actual findings, time, change from baseline and clinical concern. The school’s detailed NEWS2 scoring is taught in 7D; PEWS band details belong to the designated pediatric teaching.
依同一评分表的升级说明，同时查看单项高风险异常及总分。交接时连同实际发现、时间、基线变化及临床担忧一起说明分数。本校详细 NEWS2 计分在 7D 教授；PEWS 分组细节在指定儿科课教授。

00:25:09.216 --> 00:25:29.904
Original process drill: a child has new work of breathing and a behavior change. Identify the correct school PEWS reference, confirm the age band, collect the chart’s required observations, then explain how the result would be communicated and acted on. Do not substitute an adult NEWS2 calculation.
原创流程练习：一名儿童新出现呼吸费力和行为变化。先找出正确的学校 PEWS 参考表，确认年龄分组，收集表中所需观察，再说明如何沟通结果及采取行动。不要改用成人 NEWS2 计算。

00:25:29.904 --> 00:25:41.664
Use the school thirty-minute PAA rotation as a supervised practice block, not a thirty-minute permission to delay transport. Divide roles and rehearse the complete decision chain.
把学校三十分钟 PAA 轮转理解为督导练习时间块，不是允许延误转运三十分钟。分配角色，演练完整决策链。

00:25:41.664 --> 00:25:53.544
Have the instructor introduce a change after movement. Stop the current nonessential task, return to immediate threats, verify new measurements and revise your plan aloud.
请教师在搬动后加入一个变化。停止当前非必要任务，回到即时威胁，核实新测量，并大声修订计划。

00:25:53.544 --> 00:26:05.016
Then produce your own PCR from the observed simulation and deliver a concise transfer report. Use the documentation and communication workshops already included in this week.
随后根据实际模拟观察，自己写 PCR，并做简明交接。使用本周已包含的记录和沟通练习方法。

00:26:05.016 --> 00:26:18.000
For review, explain the reason for every priority and what finding would change it. The aim is a reproducible safe assessment, not memorizing our fictional narrative or a school quiz answer.
复盘时解释每个优先决定的理由，以及什么发现会改变它。目标是可重复的安全评估，不是背我们的虚构故事或学校测验答案。
